<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ciro Menotti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1798">1798</a>–<a href="/years/1831">1831</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ciro Menotti (1798–1831) was an Italian patriot from Carpi in the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a>. He conspired for a revolution in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and hoped for the support of Duke Francis IV, but the duke had him arrested on the eve of the revolt of February 1831. After Austrian troops restored the duke, Menotti was hanged in Modena.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ciro-menotti.jpg" alt="Ciro Menotti" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciro_Menotti_-_Malatesta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
